     "winPct": 87
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kit": [
    "aegis",
    "bishop-step",
    "decoy",
    "twin"
   ],
   "anchors": [
    "aegis+bishop-step",
    "decoy+twin"
   ],
   "reason": "The key on the king's diagonal is usually defended, which makes the bishop capture suicide; with the shield up she takes it anyway, absorbs the recapture, keeps the capture-stun and takes the king on the next move. | Same protection for the most-hunted body; the Twin's value is entirely in surviving long enough to hold a second line.",
